From 6190bb7de3ccc6c90e21e66f38c504124cdb5d33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:38:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Lab: XCL_FENCE_DIRECT=1 - XCL's own fence probes skip
 the title's GetCompletedValue hook

alloc_pool (note_resubmits, in_flight, allocator_in_flight), sparse
drain_quarantined, list_x note_internal_wait / internal_waits_summary
and vram (scrub, zeroer, retire sweep) asked their adopted fences
through the COM call, which is the title's hook: it settles copies
back, trying the sparse state's lock for ~2 ms. drain_quarantined and
note_internal_wait do so with that lock held, so the try always failed.

real::probe_completed is the COM call as before, or with the lab switch
the PC's value (real::fence_completed). Off by default. The value read
is the same; copies back still land from the title's own fence calls,
fence_wait_fired and the readback thread.

Test: an adopted WARP fence with a copy back pending and the state held
reads the same value both ways; off takes the hook's >= 2 ms, on < 1 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
